{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Each man his fire-pan.</b> Each man took his fire-pan, and in my opinion this matter was also on the eighth day, and the proof is: 'for today they offered their sin-offering.'" "<b>And they put fire in them.</b> Not from the fire that went out, and this is the meaning of 'strange fire.'" "And the meaning of <b>which He did not command them</b> is that they did it of their own mind and not by command, to offer incense, and also with strange fire."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:15.755862102Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}